● This error (src refspec main does not match any) means that after you deleted
  the .git folder and ran git init, your current branch is not actually named 
  main. In newer versions of Git, the default branch is often master.

  Since we want it to be main for Vercel and GitHub, let's fix the branch name
  and push.

  🛠️ The Final Fix (Run these exactly):

  1. Rename your current branch to main:
  git branch -M main

  2. Now, push it to GitHub:
  git push -u origin main --force

  ---

  🔍 Why this happened:

  When you ran git init, Git created a default branch (probably called master).
  When you tried to git push origin main, Git looked for a branch named main to
  send to GitHub, didn't find one, and gave you that "refspec" error.

  git branch -M main tells Git: "Rename whatever branch I'm on right now to 
  'main'."

  After you run those two commands:
  1. Refresh your GitHub page: https://github.com/Khan-coder-31/portfolio
  2. You should now see the app folder and all your files.
  3. Then, go to Vercel and deploy!

  Tell me once you see the files on GitHub!

