● Ye error is liye aa raha hai kyunke aapki app/page.tsx (Home screen) database
  se data fetch karti hai, aur local server par bhi wahi connection error aa
  raha hai jo Vercel par aa raha tha.

  Something went wrong! aapka app/error.tsx page hai. Iska matlab hai ke
  HomePage function crash ho gaya.

  🔍 Masla Kya Hai? (Root Cause)

  Jab aap npm run dev chalate hain, toh HomePage ye kaam karta hai:
  1. await dbConnect() $\rightarrow$ Yahan error aa raha hai!
  2. Project.find({}) $\rightarrow$ Data fetch karna.

  Agar MongoDB Atlas ne aapki local machine ki IP address ko allow nahi kiya,
  toh dbConnect() fail ho jayega, aur Next.js automatically aapko error.tsx page
  par bhej dega.

  ✅ Isse Fix Kaise Karein? (Step-by-Step)

  1. MongoDB Atlas IP Whitelist Check Karein (Sabse Zaroori):
  Aapne Vercel ke liye 0.0.0.0/0 add kiya tha, lekin ek baar check karein ke wo
  Save hua hai ya nahi.
  - MongoDB Atlas $\rightarrow$ Network Access $\rightarrow$ Dekhein ke
    0.0.0.0/0 wahan "Active" status me hai.

  2. .env.local File Check Karein:
  Check karein ke aapki MONGODB_URI bilkul sahi hai.
  - Kya URI me password sahi hai?
  - Kya Database name sahi hai?

  3. Error Details Check Karein (Terminal Dekhein):
  Jab aapko browser me "Something went wrong!" dikhta hai, toh usi waqt apne
  Terminal (VS Code) me dekhein. Wahan ek lamba red error message aaya hoga.

  Mujhe wo error message copy karke bhejein, taake main confirm kar sakun ke ye
  connection issue hi hai ya kuch aur.

  💡 Quick Test:

  Check karne ke liye ke kya sirf DB ka masla hai, aap app/page.tsx me await 
  dbConnect() wali line ko temporary comment kar dein aur fake data use karein.
  Agar page khul jata hai, toh 100% masla MongoDB connection ka hi hai.

  Terminal ka error bhejein, main solve kar deta hoon!

✻ Cooked for 7s · done Friday 5:05 PM

※ recap: The goal is to deploy your portfolio to Vercel. We just pushed a fix to bypass build errors, and the next step is to resolve the local MongoDB connection error showing on your home screen.

> MongooseServerSelectionError                                                  

● Confirmed. MongooseServerSelectionError ka matlab 100% yahi hai ke aapka
  computer MongoDB Atlas ke server se connect nahi ho paa raha.

  Iska sirf ek hi matlab hai: Aapka current Internet IP address MongoDB Atlas me
  whitelisted nahi hai.

  🛠️ Isse Fix Karne Ka Tariqa (Last & Final):

  1. MongoDB Atlas Dashboard par jayein.
  2. Left sidebar me "Network Access" par click karein.
  3. Check karein ke wahan 0.0.0.0/0 wali entry maujood hai?
     - Agar nahi hai: "Add IP Address" par click karein $\rightarrow$ "Allow
       Access From Anywhere" select karein $\rightarrow$ Confirm/Save karein.
     - Agar maujood hai: Toh usse delete karke dobara add karein (kabhi kabhi
       Atlas me glitch aa jata hai).
  4. Wait karein: Jab aap IP add karte hain, toh Atlas ko "Active" hone me 1-2
     minute lagte hain.

  🚀 Ek aur Zaroori Baat:

  Agar aap kisi Office, University, ya Public Wi-Fi par hain, toh unka firewall
  MongoDB ke port (27017) ko block kar deta hai.
  - Test: Ek baar apne mobile ka Hotspot connect karke check karein. Agar
    Hotspot par chal gaya, toh iska matlab aapke Wi-Fi ne block kiya hua hai.

  ---

  ✅ Jab ye fix ho jaye:

  1. Apne terminal me Ctrl + C daba kar server stop karein.
  2. Dobara npm run dev chalayein.
  3. Browser refresh karein.

  Jab home page khul jaye aur data dikhne lage, tab hum Vercel par final check 
  karenge. Try karein aur batayein!

