✻ Sautéed for 10s · done Friday 5:53 PM

> bro I placed the favicon png directly in portfolio/                           

● It needs to be in the public folder, not the main portfolio folder.

  In Next.js, any image, font, or icon that you want the browser to see (like a
  favicon) MUST be inside the public directory. If it's just in the main
  portfolio folder, the website cannot "see" it.

  🛠️ Quick Fix:

  Please move the file from D:\portfolio\favicon.png to
  D:\portfolio\public\favicon.png.

  If you can't find the folder, you can run this command in your terminal to 
  move it for you:

  mv favicon.png public/favicon.png

  Once you have moved it, tell me "Done" and I will push the code to GitHub so 
  your live site gets the icon!
