  🚀 Next Task: Advanced Animation Polish

  Now that the page transitions are working, let's make the content inside the 
  pages feel more alive.

  Right now, your sections (Hero, Projects, Experience) probably appear all at
  once or with very simple animations. I want to implement "Scroll-Triggered 
  Animations".

  What this means:
  Instead of everything appearing immediately, the elements will "slide in" or
  "fade up" exactly when they enter the user's viewport as they scroll down the
  page. This is what makes a site feel "expensive" and high-end.

  My plan for this step:
  1. I will review your Hero.tsx, Projects.tsx, and Experience.tsx components.
  2. I'll refine the initial and whileInView properties of the Framer Motion
     components.
  3. I'll add a subtle stagger effect, so that if you have 3 project cards, they
     don't all pop up at once, but one-by-one (1... 2... 3...).

  I'll start by analyzing the current animations in your components. Let's go!
  🎨✨

