● I've started the Animation Polish by refining the Hero section.

  I noticed your Hero animations were using a basic duration timer. I've
  replaced that for the main heading with a Spring Transition.

  🌟 What is a "Spring" transition?

  Instead of a robotic, linear movement, a spring transition mimics real-world
  physics. The text will now "bounce" slightly into place, which makes the
  website feel more dynamic and high-end.

  I've just updated components/sections/Hero.tsx with:
  - type: "spring"
  - stiffness: 100
  - damping: 20

  🛠️ Next up: The Project Cards & Experience Timeline

  I'm now going to update Projects.tsx and Experience.tsx to implement Staggered
  Viewport Animations.

  This means:
  1. The cards won't just appear; they will slide up one after another
     (1... 2... 3...) as you scroll down.
  2. I'll use whileInView so the animation only triggers when the user actually
     reaches that section.

  I'm moving to Projects.tsx now! 🚀

